{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Nth Bell number, B(n), which is the number of partitions of a set with n elements.\n    Uses dynamic programming based on the Bell triangle construction.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # `bell_row` stores the elements of the previous row (i-1) of the Bell triangle.\n    # Initially, it represents the 0-th row, which contains only B(0).\n    bell_row = [1] \n\n    # Iterate from the first row (i=1) up to the Nth row.\n    # Each iteration computes the (i)-th row of the Bell triangle.\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Create a new list for the current row (i).\n        # The (i)-th row will have i+1 elements.\n        next_row = [0] * (i + 1)\n        \n        # The first element of the current row (T[i][0]) is the last element\n        # of the previous row (T[i-1][i-1]). This value is B(i).\n        next_row[0] = bell_row[-1]\n        \n        # Fill the rest of the current row using the recurrence T[i][j] = T[i][j-1] + T[i-1][j-1].\n        # T[i][j-1] is `next_row[j-1]` (element to the left in current row).\n        # T[i-1][j-1] is `bell_row[j-1]` (element above in previous row).\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            next_row[j] = next_row[j-1] + bell_row[j-1]\n        \n        # Update `bell_row` to be the newly computed current row.\n        bell_row = next_row\n    \n    # After N iterations, `bell_row` contains the Nth row of the Bell triangle,\n    # where its first element (T[N][0]) is B(N).\n    return bell_row[0]"}
