{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "def reverse_vowels(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses only the vowels in the input string, preserving the positions of non-vowel characters.\n    Vowels are defined as 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u' (case-insensitive), excluding 'y'.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _is_vowel(char: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a given character is a vowel according to the system rules.\n        \"\"\"\n        return char.lower() in 'aeiou'\n\n    char_list = list(input_string)\n    vowel_indices = []\n    collected_vowels = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(char_list):\n        if _is_vowel(char):\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n            collected_vowels.append(char)\n\n    if not collected_vowels:\n        return input_string\n\n    collected_vowels.reverse()\n\n    for i, vowel_char in zip(vowel_indices, collected_vowels):\n        char_list[i] = vowel_char\n\n    return \"\".join(char_list)"}
