{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of the given number to 1.\n    Odd-indexed bits retain their original values.\n    \"\"\"\n    mask = 0\n    # Determine the maximum bit position to consider for the mask.\n    # This covers up to the highest bit set in 'number' (its bit_length) plus a buffer for the next even bit.\n    max_bit_pos = number.bit_length()\n\n    # Generate a mask with 1s at all even bit positions.\n    # The range ensures coverage for relevant bits based on the number's magnitude.\n    for i in range(0, max_bit_pos + 2, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply the mask using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return number | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\n    Handles negative numbers by considering 0 as the next perfect square.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    int_root = int(math.isqrt(number))\n    next_root = int_root + 1\n    return next_root * next_root"}
