{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    This uses dynamic programming with a 2D table.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_string)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Substrings of length 1 have an LPS of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for increasing substring lengths\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1 # End index of current substring\n\n            if input_string[i] == input_string[j]:\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + dp[i+1][j-1]\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
