{"task_id": "Mbpp/266", "solution": "class Cube:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents a cube and provides methods to calculate its geometric properties.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, side_length: float):\n        \"\"\"\n        Initializes a Cube instance with the given side length.\n        \"\"\"\n        self._side_length = side_length\n\n    def calculate_lateral_surface_area(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Computes the lateral surface area of the cube.\n        \"\"\"\n        return 4 * (self._side_length ** 2)\ndef lateralsurface_cube(side_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a cube given its side length.\n    \"\"\"\n    cube = Cube(side_length)\n    return cube.calculate_lateral_surface_area()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "def list_split(input_list: list, n: int) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Splits an input list into n sub-lists, distributing elements by their index modulo n.\n    Returns a list of the resulting sub-lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    output_list = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n    for i, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        target_sublist_index = i % n\n        output_list[target_sublist_index].append(element)\n    return output_list"}
