{"task_id": "Mbpp/281", "solution": "def all_unique(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if all elements in the given list are unique.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The list to check for unique elements.\n\n    Returns:\n        True if all elements are unique, False otherwise.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> all_unique([1, 2, 3])\n        True\n        >>> all_unique([1, 2, 2])\n        False\n    \"\"\"\n    # Using a set to efficiently check for duplicates.\n    # A list has unique elements if its length equals the length of a set\n    # created from its elements (as sets only store unique elements).\n    return len(input_list) == len(set(input_list))"}
