{"task_id": "Mbpp/293", "solution": "import math\ndef otherside_rightangle(leg1_length: float, leg2_length: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the hypotenuse of a right-angled triangle using the Pythagorean theorem.\n    Validates inputs and rounds the result to 14 decimal places.\n    \"\"\"\n    if leg1_length <= 0 or leg2_length <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Leg lengths must be positive numbers.\")\n\n    hypotenuse_squared = leg1_length**2 + leg2_length**2\n    hypotenuse = math.sqrt(hypotenuse_squared)\n\n    return round(hypotenuse, 14)"}
