{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts inversions in an array using merge sort.\n    An inversion is a pair (i, j) where i < j and arr[i] > arr[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return 0\n\n    def _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr, temp_arr, left, right):\n        \"\"\"Recursively sorts and counts inversions in subarrays.\"\"\"\n        inversions = 0\n        if left < right:\n            mid = (left + right) // 2\n            inversions += _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr, temp_arr, left, mid)\n            inversions += _merge_sort_and_count(current_arr, temp_arr, mid + 1, right)\n            inversions += _merge(current_arr, temp_arr, left, mid, right)\n        return inversions\n\n    def _merge(current_arr, temp_arr, left, mid, right):\n        \"\"\"Merges two sorted subarrays and counts inversions crossing the midpoint.\"\"\"\n        inv_count = 0\n\n        # Copies current subarray to temp_arr for merging.\n        for k in range(left, right + 1):\n            temp_arr[k] = current_arr[k]\n\n        i = left      # Pointer for left part of temp_arr.\n        j = mid + 1   # Pointer for right part of temp_arr.\n        k = left      # Pointer for original current_arr.\n\n        while i <= mid and j <= right:\n            if temp_arr[i] <= temp_arr[j]:\n                current_arr[k] = temp_arr[i]\n                i += 1\n            else:\n                current_arr[k] = temp_arr[j]\n                j += 1\n                # If temp_arr[i] > temp_arr[j], it signifies inversions with remaining elements in the left subarray.\n                inv_count += (mid - i + 1)\n            k += 1\n\n        # Copies remaining elements from left subarray.\n        while i <= mid:\n            current_arr[k] = temp_arr[i]\n            i += 1\n            k += 1\n\n        # Copies remaining elements from right subarray.\n        while j <= right:\n            current_arr[k] = temp_arr[j]\n            j += 1\n            k += 1\n            \n        return inv_count\n\n    temp_arr = [0] * n\n    return _merge_sort_and_count(arr, temp_arr, 0, n - 1)"}
