{"task_id": "Mbpp/300", "solution": "import math\ndef count_binary_seq(n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of binary sequences of length 2n such that\n    the sum of the first n bits is the same as the sum of the last n bits.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_count = 0.0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        combinations_for_k = math.comb(n, k)\n        total_count += combinations_for_k * combinations_for_k\n    return total_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "def max_aggregate(data: list[tuple[str, int]]) -> tuple[str, int]:\n    # Aggregates scores for each unique name and finds the name with the highest total score.\n    # Returns a tuple containing that name and its highest aggregate score.\n    aggregated_scores = {}\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] = aggregated_scores.get(name, 0) + score\n\n    max_name = ''\n    max_score = float('-inf') # Initialize with a very small number\n\n    for name, total_score in aggregated_scores.items():\n        if total_score > max_score:\n            max_score = total_score\n            max_name = name\n\n    # Handle the edge case of an empty input list or if all scores sum to negative infinity\n    # based on the problem's context, assuming non-empty input that leads to a valid result.\n    if max_score == float('-inf'):\n        return '', 0 # Or handle based on specific empty input requirements, defaulting to 0 for score.\n\n    return max_name, max_score"}
