{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "def min_val(input_list: list) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n    Non-numeric items are ignored during the search process.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_elements = []\n    for item in input_list:\n        try:\n            # Attempt to convert the item to a float.\n            # This implicitly filters out non-numeric types that cannot be converted.\n            numeric_elements.append(float(item))\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            # If conversion fails, the item is considered non-numeric and is ignored.\n            pass\n\n    if not numeric_elements:\n        # If no numeric elements are found, positive infinity is returned\n        # as a non-raising way to indicate no minimum could be determined.\n        return float('inf')\n    else:\n        return min(numeric_elements)"}
