{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    This function uses memoization to efficiently compute Perrin numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    _memo = {}\n\n    def _get_perrin_number(k: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively calculates the k-th Perrin number, memoizing results.\n        Perrin numbers are defined as P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(k)=P(k-2)+P(k-3) for k > 2.\n        \"\"\"\n        if k in _memo:\n            return _memo[k]\n        \n        if k == 0:\n            result = 3\n        elif k == 1:\n            result = 0\n        elif k == 2:\n            result = 2\n        else:\n            result = _get_perrin_number(k - 2) + _get_perrin_number(k - 3)\n        \n        _memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        total_sum += _get_perrin_number(i)\n    \n    return total_sum"}
