{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(nums: list) -> float:\n    # Initialize variables to keep track of max and min products ending at the current position,\n    # and the overall maximum product found so far.\n    if not nums:\n        return 0.0\n\n    max_so_far = float(nums[0])\n    min_so_far = float(nums[0])\n    result = float(nums[0])\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nums)):\n        current_num = float(nums[i])\n        \n        # Calculate the potential new max_so_far and min_so_far.\n        # temp_max stores the max_so_far before it's updated, so it can be used for min_so_far calculation.\n        temp_max = max(current_num, max_so_far * current_num, min_so_far * current_num)\n        min_so_far = min(current_num, max_so_far * current_num, min_so_far * current_num)\n        \n        max_so_far = temp_max\n        \n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n        \n    return result"}
