{"task_id": "Mbpp/472", "solution": "def check_Consecutive(numbers: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the given list contains consecutive numbers.\"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # BR2: Sort the list.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n\n    # BR5: Check for duplicates.\n    if len(sorted_numbers) != len(set(sorted_numbers)):\n        return False\n\n    # BR3: Iterate and compare elements.\n    for i in range(1, len(sorted_numbers)):\n        if sorted_numbers[i] != sorted_numbers[i-1] + 1:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def tuple_intersection(list1: list[tuple], list2: list[tuple]) -> set[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple list irrespective of their order.\"\"\"\n\n    def _normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> frozenset:\n        \"\"\"Converts a tuple into a canonical, order-agnostic frozenset.\"\"\"\n        return frozenset(t)\n\n    normalized_list1_map = {}\n    for raw_tuple in list1:\n        normalized_form = _normalize_tuple(raw_tuple)\n        normalized_list1_map[normalized_form] = raw_tuple\n\n    normalized_list2_set = set()\n    for raw_tuple in list2:\n        normalized_form = _normalize_tuple(raw_tuple)\n        normalized_list2_set.add(normalized_form)\n\n    intersection_normalized_forms = set(normalized_list1_map.keys()) & normalized_list2_set\n\n    result_set = set()\n    for norm_form in intersection_normalized_forms:\n        result_set.add(normalized_list1_map[norm_form])\n\n    return result_set"}
