{"task_id": "Mbpp/557", "solution": "def toggle_string(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Toggles the case of all alphabetic characters in a string, leaving non-alphabetic characters unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    toggled_chars = []\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isupper():\n            toggled_chars.append(char.lower())\n        elif char.islower():\n            toggled_chars.append(char.upper())\n        else:\n            toggled_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(toggled_chars)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/556", "solution": "def find_Odd_Pair(input_list: list[int], list_size: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts pairs in a list whose bitwise XOR sum is odd.\n    It iterates through all unique pairs and checks their XOR sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_xor_pair_count = 0\n\n    for i in range(list_size):\n        for j in range(i + 1, list_size):\n            # Calculate xor_sum for the pair\n            xor_sum = input_list[i] ^ input_list[j]\n\n            # Check if xor_sum is odd (a number is odd if its least significant bit is 1)\n            if (xor_sum & 1) != 0:\n                odd_xor_pair_count += 1\n\n    return odd_xor_pair_count"}
