{"task_id": "Mbpp/612", "solution": "def merge(input_list: list[list]) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transforms a list of two-element sublists into a list of two lists.\n    The first output list contains the first element of each sublist,\n    and the second output list contains the second element of each sublist.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_elements = [sublist[0] for sublist in input_list]\n    second_elements = [sublist[1] for sublist in input_list]\n    return [first_elements, second_elements]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "import math\ndef prime_num(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given integer is a prime number.\n    Returns True if n is prime, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    if n == 2:\n        return True\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True"}
