{"task_id": "Mbpp/626", "solution": "def triangle_area(radius: float) -> float | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the area of the largest triangle that can be inscribed in a semicircle.\n    Returns the area of the largest inscribed triangle as a float if radius > 0, otherwise None.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius <= 0:\n        return None\n\n    # The largest triangle has its base along the diameter and its apex on the arc.\n    base = 2 * radius\n    height = radius\n    area = 0.5 * base * height\n\n    return area"}
