{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\"\"\"\n    import math\n\n    def _calculate_digits(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the number of digits in a positive integer.\"\"\"\n        return int(math.log10(number)) + 1\n\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_value = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        num_digits = _calculate_digits(triangular_value)\n        \n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n        \n        k += 1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple to a dictionary using adjacent elements.\n\n    The element at an even index becomes a key, and the subsequent odd-indexed\n    element becomes its value. If the tuple has an odd number of elements,\n    the last element is ignored.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple) - 1, 2):\n        key = input_tuple[i]\n        value = input_tuple[i+1]\n        result[key] = value\n    return result"}
