{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: PyList[Any], rotation_amount: int) -> PyList[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a given list by a specified number of items to the right.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The list of generic items to be rotated.\n        rotation_amount: The non-negative integer number of items to rotate.\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list, which is the input_list rotated to the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n\n    if rotation_amount == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    effective_rotation = rotation_amount % list_length\n\n    if effective_rotation == 0:\n        return list(input_list)\n\n    rotated_part = input_list[-effective_rotation:]\n    remaining_part = input_list[:-effective_rotation]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
