{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds numbers within a given range where every number is divisible by every digit it contains.\n\n    Raises ValueError if startnum is greater than endnum.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_self_divisible(number: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a single number is divisible by all its non-zero digits.\"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return False  # 0 is not considered self-divisible by its digits.\n        if 0 < number < 10:\n            return True   # Single digit numbers (1-9) are always self-divisible.\n\n        temp_num = number\n        while temp_num > 0:\n            digit = temp_num % 10\n            if digit == 0 or number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n            temp_num //= 10\n        return True\n\n    if startnum > endnum:\n        raise ValueError(\"startnum must be less than or equal to endnum\")\n\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if _is_self_divisible(num):\n            result.append(num)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/748", "solution": "def capital_words_spaces(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Processes the input string to insert spaces before capital letters.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string: The string to be processed.\n\n    Returns:\n        The string with spaces inserted according to the rule.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    result_chars = [input_string[0]]\n    for char in input_string[1:]:\n        if char.isupper():\n            result_chars.append(' ')\n        result_chars.append(char)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
